/*****************************************************************************
    enumT -- THE ENUM-TRANSITION CONFIRMATION ROW. 2026-08-17.

    Ruling 2 (Tony): compile tests isCoded; success transitions isCoded to
    isAction; failure leaves the state untouched with processCode complaining
    loud. The consequence that matters is that WALK-WRITES AND PARSER-READS
    CANNOT DISAGREE BY CONSTRUCTION -- walkRules gates on actionTypE while
    parseRule tests isAction, and if those could drift apart the whole grammar
    could generate, install, and be silently ignored at exit 0.

    ⚠ THIS ROW EXISTS BECAUSE DESIGNED IS NOT DEMONSTRATED. The mechanism was
    found already implemented -- processCode's success arm carries
    `field.isAction = true` and its own comment says it overwrites actionType
    and consumes isCoded -- so nothing needed writing. That is exactly the
    situation where a confirmation row is worth its cost and an assumption is
    not: the design says it happens, and this says it happened.

    ⚠ WHY isActioN AND NOT actionTypE. actionTypE reads NONZERO for isAction OR
    isCoded, so it cannot tell the two apart and would pass identically before
    and after the transition -- a row that moves for neither reason. isActioN
    reads the flag parseRule ACTUALLY tests. Without it this fixture would be
    the vacuous kind it is meant to prevent.

    THE THREE ROWS:
      A  before compile -- the subject carries code but has not been compiled,
         so isActioN must be 0 and actionTypE must be 1. That PAIR is the
         discriminator: 1 and 0 together prove the state is isCoded and not
         merely empty, which neither number alone can say.
      B  compile returns the field (it accepted an isCoded subject).
      C  after compile -- isActioN must be 1. The transition happened, so the
         arm the walk creates IS the arm the parser reads.
*****************************************************************************/

register(EnumSubj);
define
    etMark;
    etSubject code={ etMark = 7; };
    ;

register(EnumProbe);
define
    etProbe code={
        a := etSubject.actionTypE;
        b := etSubject.isActioN;
        print "A  before compile: actionTypE =" a " isActioN =" b " (want 1 and 0 -- isCoded, not empty)":;
        r := compile(etSubject);
        if r;
            print "B  compile returned a field on the isCoded subject":;
        else
            print "B  FAIL compile returned null":;
        c := etSubject.isActioN;
        print "C  after  compile: isActioN =" c " (want 1 -- the transition parseRule reads)":;
        };
    ;

etProbe();
print "ENUMT SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
